    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `POST /api/owners` (and every owner read) return a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo files touched, each with a minimal, cohesive edit:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` line on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\n**Structural impact:** The only Java method changed is the abstract `toOwnerDto` (CC = 1, with tiny surrounding `WMC_other`), and the edit is a single annotation line \u2014 no method or class was grown, and no controller/service logic was touched. The formatting lives declaratively in the mapper where DTO projection already belongs.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
